me from the first family of American snowboarding. In 2005 she had been featured in a snowboarding documentary, " [:em {} "First Descent"] ", which also starred " [:a {:href "/athletes/109860"} "Shaun White"] " and Norwegian snowboarding legend Terje Håkonsen. All three Americans easily made it thru the qualifying, which was led by Clark, with the top European, Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/101107"} "Kjersti Buaas"] ", joining them, along with the fourth American, " [:a {:href "/athletes/109976"} "Elena Hight"] ". Both Buaas and Hight needed their second run to qualify. The final was dominated not by Bleiler, as expected, but by Hannah Teter, who posted the top score on both runs. Her first run of 44.6 was good enough for the gold medal, but she surpassed it in run two with a 46.4. Bleiler hung on for second, placing second in both runs. Clark was in third after the first run, but Buaas improved to 42.0 in the second to move up to the bronze medal and break up the American sweep."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying Round 1"] [:th {} "Qualifying Round 2"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/109966"} "Hannah Teter"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "39.9 (3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "46.4 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/109965"} "Gretchen Bleiler"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "41.6 (2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td